# Stitch design artifacts

`stitch_e-commerce/stitch/` is the original Stitch export (static HTML screens + `@stitch_e-commerce/stitch/everest_commerce/DESIGN.md`). The running app is SvelteKit under `src/`.

## Do

- Read `DESIGN.md` and the matching `code.html` when porting a screen (homepage, catalog, PDP, cart, checkout, account, journal, about).
- Recreate the screen as a Svelte route using tokens from `@src/routes/layout.css` and existing `$lib` components/stores.
- Keep editorial copy and layout ideas, but wire behavior to mock stores (cart, checkout, auth, orders).

## Do not

- Do not import or serve Stitch HTML from SvelteKit.
- Do not paste Stitch markup unchanged (it will not have runes, `$lib` stores, or theme utilities).
- Do not add a second design-token source. If Stitch hex values differ, prefer the mapped `@theme` names already used in the app.
- Do not commit zip duplicates of this folder (`*.zip` is gitignored).
